The spouses E operate in the agricultural zone of the municipality Q (Canton Y) an agricultural holding that has existed for several generations (an agricultural enterprise within the meaning of the Federal Act on Rural Land Law). In addition to 30 dairy cows and 100 chickens, they also keep a few donkeys, goats and rabbits. The feed required for the animals is produced on their own land. Part of the remaining area is used for vegetable and fruit growing. All farm buildings located on their land are in use and offer no room for additional uses. On their land, about two kilometres away from the farm, there is also a grain mill built in the 19th century, whose tenants gave up the business in 2017 and which has stood empty since then.

To supplement their income somewhat, the spouses E plan:

- a 3 m high and 10 m2 small hut between the dwelling house and the cow barn, which is to serve for the sale (self-service) of the farm’s own products such as milk, eggs, fresh vegetables and fruit as well as home-made jam, etc.;

- a three-storey extension to the barn, modelled in design on the barn, with three bedrooms and associated sanitary facilities on a total area of 60 m2, for rental to holiday guests (half board). Here families with children – combined with an attractive supporting programme – are to spend adventure holidays on the farm. In high season, the spouses E would depend on a part-time employee to assist them in running the guesthouse;

- an excursion restaurant in the disused mill, which requires major structural alterations inside the building and to the façade. The restaurant is to be – as the mill previously was – leased out.
